            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A wireless device (406), based on the at least one first logical channel having data available for uplink transmission, is configured to set a first counter, of a first SR configuration, to a first initial value; to increment the first counter based on transmission of a first SR associated with the at least one first logical channel; and to transmit a random access preamble in response to the first counter reaching a first counter value. Based on at least one second logical channel having data available for uplink transmission, the wireless device is also configured to set a second counter, of a second SR configuration, to a second initial value; to increment the second counter based on transmission of a second SR associated with the at least one second logical channel; and to transmit a random access preamble in response to the second counter reaching a second counter value.</p>
            </abstract>
